# One lane's floor, tiled down the screen. 50x32 at 2x fills the 100px lane.
#
# Mostly transparent, which is the whole point. An opaque lane floor covered
# the sun completely — the board is 400px of a 640px window, dead centre, so a
# solid lane hides exactly the thing the backdrop was drawn for.
#
# The knock-back is a Bayer dither of night-1 at about 40%, which is how this
# era did translucency and the only way to do it here: alpha is binary
# (STYLE.md), so a partially-transparent lane has to be a partially-*absent*
# one. It darkens the grid enough for the aqua notes to hold their contrast
# while the horizon still reads through.
#
# The ruler line every 8 rows is static and gives the eye something to judge a
# falling note's speed against.
name rhythm-lane
size 50 32
key L grid-dim
key m night-3-rim
key n night-1
pixels
LLmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmLL
LL...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n..LL
LLn.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.LL
LL.n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...nLL
LLn.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.LL
LL...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n..LL
LLn.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.n.LL
LL.n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...n...nLL
